{"lemma":"שׁוּט","translit":"shûwṭ","pronunciation":"shoot","def":"properly, to push forth; (but used only figuratively) to lash, i.e. (the sea with oars) to row; by implication, to travel","kjv":"go (about, through, to and fro), mariner, rower, run to and fro.","occ":[[9,24,8,"So when they had gone","strongMorph:TH8799"],[25,27,26,"Thy rowers","strongMorph:TH8801"],[23,5,1,"Run ye to and fro","strongMorph:TH8786"],[3,11,8,"went about","strongMorph:TH8804"],[13,16,9,"run to and fro","strongMorph:TH8789"],[25,27,8,"were thy mariners","strongMorph:TH8801"],[9,24,2,"with him, Go now through","strongMorph:TH8798"],[29,8,12,"they shall run to and fro","strongMorph:TH8787"],[26,12,4,"shall run to and fro","strongMorph:TH8787"],[17,1,7,"From going to and fro","strongMorph:TH8800"],[17,2,2,"From going to and fro","strongMorph:TH8800"],[23,49,3,"and run to and fro","strongMorph:TH8708"],[37,4,10,"which run to and fro","strongMorph:TH8789"]]}